================================================================================
Third-party material adapted into traminex
================================================================================

Current-source status (2026-07-22): the ten modules inventoried below were
independently reimplemented from the exact vendored TraMineR 2.2-14 and
TraMineRextras 0.6.9 authorities (and the exact WeightedCluster 2.0 ASW source
where TraMineR delegates that statistic). No current implementation in those
modules is adapted from Sequenzo. The following inventory and license text are
retained unchanged as historical provenance for earlier revisions; its
present-tense wording describes those historical revisions, not the current
source tree.

This product includes software adapted from Sequenzo
(https://github.com/Liang-Team/Sequenzo), licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.

Portions of the following traminex modules are adapted (not verbatim copies) from
Sequenzo source. Each such module carries an attribution header; the numerics were
re-verified against live TraMineR / TraMineRextras and the public symbols renamed
to their TraMineR-faithful names:

  - traminex/multidomain_cat.py
        adapted from sequenzo/multidomain/cat.py
        (CAT combined-OM multidomain: seqdistmc / seqMD)

  - traminex/diss_mfa.py
        adapted from sequenzo/discrepancy_analysis/stats/multifactor_association.py
        (weighted multi-factor analysis of a distance matrix: dissmfacw)

  - traminex/seqemlt.py
        adapted from sequenzo/emlt/seqemlt.py
        (EMLT situations/profiles/coordinates/correlations: seqemlt)

  - traminex/disstree_helpers.py
        adapted from sequenzo/discrepancy_analysis/trees/tree_leaf_helpers.py
        (tree leaf membership / classification rules / assignment:
        disstreeleaf / disstree_get_rules / disstree_assign)

  - traminex/disstree_viz.py
        adapted from sequenzo/discrepancy_analysis/trees/tree_visualization.py
        (the optional-graphviz / graceful-fallback mechanism and node-recursion
        shape of the tree display helpers: disstree2dotp / seqtree2dot /
        disstreedisplay / seqtreedisplay; the DOT bytes follow TraMineR directly)

  - traminex/diss_indic.py
        adapted from sequenzo/discrepancy_analysis/stats/individual_indicators.py
        (individual diss-based marginality / gain indicators: dissindic)

  - traminex/diss_merge.py
        the greedy merge control-flow shape follows
        sequenzo/discrepancy_analysis/stats/merge_cluster_groups.py
        (group merging by ASW quality: dissmergegroups). The ASW itself follows
        WeightedCluster / TraMineR directly (Sequenzo's own ASW helper is not
        faithful to WeightedCluster::wcClusterQuality and was not used).

  - traminex/domassoc.py
        adapted from sequenzo/multidomain/association_between_domains.py
        (cross-domain position-wise LRT / Cramer's V association: seqdomassoc)

  - traminex/repseq_rf.py
        adapted from sequenzo/representative_sequences.py
        (relative-frequency groups + representatives: dissrf / seqrf). The
        weighted "prop" frequency grouping follows TraMineR dissrf.R / seqrf.R.

  - cpp/src/accel_kernels.h
        adapted from sequenzo/dissimilarity_measures/src/
        {HAMdistance,LCSdistance,OMdistance}.cpp and dp_utils.h
        (the OpenMP-parallel pairwise loop and the per-pair OM / LCS / HAM
        edit-distance kernels behind seqdist -- a speed accelerator gated on
        byte-identity, atol=0, to traminex's pure-Python kernels). The OMspell
        sub-family and the xsimd vectorisation paths are deliberately not
        borrowed; normalisation and deduplication remain in traminex's Python
        layer (the kernels return raw distances).

